From: Project contributors <contributors@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] outbound: read Vision UDP replies into 64 KiB buffers

vision.PacketConn.ReadFrom rejected a payload when
length > uint16(len(p)). dae's DNS forwarder reads UDP replies into a
65536-byte buffer, which uint16() wraps to 0, so every reply through an
xtls-rprx-vision node was drained and returned as io.ErrShortBuffer.
dae logged "DNS forward to upstream failed ... error=short buffer
network=udp+4", fell back to TCP for each query and kept marking the
node's udp4(DNS) dead and alive again.

Compare the lengths as int, and add a regression test. The library is
the module that dae-wing and dae core already pin
(github.com/olicesx/outbound v0.0.0-sticky-ip.0.20260918090140-cc86ced2e683,
unpacked to third_party/outbound by the recipe); both go.mod replace
directives now point at that copy. Upstream outbound has the same check.
---
